From b97b2605f2199962efa26b070c55e80b037237a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:42:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] eip155: report a Permit2 spender other than the exact
 proxy as invalid_payload
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

assert_offchain_valid reported a permit whose spender is not the x402 exact
proxy as RecipientMismatch, i.e. invalid_exact_evm_payload_recipient_mismatch.
The spender never receives funds: the proxy is what binds the transfer to the
witness's recipient, so another spender makes the payload unusable, which x402
v2 §9 calls invalid_payload ("Payment payload is malformed or contains invalid
data").

The spender is now checked by assert_exact_proxy_spender, before the
signature: the signature's EIP-712 hash is built with the proxy as spender, so
checking the signature first reported such a payload as an invalid signature
rather than for what is wrong with it. The TS reference facilitator also checks
the spender before the signature (permit2.ts).
